==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr}} {{term|révolter|lang=fr}}, from {{etyl|it}} {{term|rivoltare|lang=it}}, from {{etyl|VL.}} *{{term||revolvitāre}}, frequentative of {{etyl|la}} {{term|revolvo|revolvō|roll back|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|En-us-revolt.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|əʊlt}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|revolts|revolting|revolted|revolted}}

# to [[rebel]], particularly against authority
#: ''The farmers had to '''revolt''' against the government to get what they deserved.''
# to greatly [[repel]]
#: ''Your brother ''revolts'' me!''

